# Public types that may move between src/ assemblies in this PR WITHOUT a type forwarder.
#
# An entry is a STATEMENT THAT NO SHIPPED MODULE CAN BE HOLDING THAT TypeRef — not a way to make
# the gate quiet. A module's IL binds `Namespace.Type` scoped to an AssemblyRef, so moving a public
# type between assemblies (or renaming its namespace) is binary-breaking for every module compiled
# earlier: it dies with `TypeLoadException: Could not load type '…'` the moment the platform rolls.
# That is #2370 — it took down the whole /mcp surface of a production deployment.
#
# The FIX is normally a forwarder, not an entry here:
#
#     [assembly: TypeForwardedTo(typeof(Old.Namespace.TheType))]     // in src/<OldAssembly>
#
# and, because a forwarder cannot rename, the type keeps its ORIGINAL full name in its new home.
#
# One `Assembly:Namespace.Type` per line, then the PULL REQUEST this entry travels with, then a
# reason:
#
#   MeshWeaver.Foo:MeshWeaver.Foo.Widget  #1234 — added and moved inside one unreleased wave
#
# 🚨 AN ENTRY IS TRANSITIONAL AND EXPIRES BY MECHANISM, not by anyone remembering (#3422).
#
#   * It is in force ONLY in the diff that ADDS it. The moment it merges, the line stops being
#     an addition, and every later pull request treats it as INERT: it permits nothing, and it
#     fails nothing. There is nothing here for you to delete on a later day — deleting a landed
#     line is tidying, never a fix.
#   * The `#<number>` is a PULL REQUEST in this repository and the gate resolves it. Open, and
#     the allowance stands. Merged, closed-unmerged, an issue, missing, or unresolvable, and the
#     gate goes RED naming which: "could not tell" never renders as "allowed".
#   * An entry that permits nothing in the diff that adds it still FAILS — on that diff, which
#     is its author's own pull request.
#
# The line this replaces read "DELETE the line once the change has shipped". Nobody did, once;
# for ~40 minutes every C#-touching pull request in the fleet was red on somebody else's merge.
# See Doc/Architecture/TransitionalAllowEntries.

# #7118 — IModuleUpdatePolicy is DELETED, not moved: retired 2026-09-14, registered and consumed by
# nothing since; no fleet repository names it (Systemorph org code search) and the per-partition
# in-mesh sweep on systemorph and control found no Code/NodeType node naming it. A module compiled
# against an earlier platform that still bound it is reported Unlinkable (ModulePlatformLink).
MeshWeaver.PluginCatalog:MeshWeaver.PluginCatalog.IModuleUpdatePolicy  #7118 — deleted, not moved; no caller in the fleet or the live mesh

# #7147 — NotOwnedServiceDescriptorExtensions and ReflectionCacheEviction are DELETED with Autofac,
# not moved: the first populated an Autofac ContainerBuilder (PopulateMeshWeaver's signature takes
# one), the second purged Autofac's reflection caches on load-context unload — no forwarder can
# keep either without keeping Autofac. Their only callers were core's own (ModuleLoadContext,
# CompilationCacheService); no fleet repository names them (git grep over origin/main of
# MeshWeaver.Plugins, .Education, .Reinsurance, .SocialMedia, .Manufacturing, .Crm and Memex: 0
# files). A module compiled against an earlier platform that still bound one is reported
# Unlinkable (ModulePlatformLink).
MeshWeaver.ServiceProvider:MeshWeaver.ServiceProvider.NotOwnedServiceDescriptorExtensions  #7147 — deleted with Autofac, not moved; signature is Autofac's ContainerBuilder; no caller outside core
MeshWeaver.ServiceProvider:MeshWeaver.ServiceProvider.ReflectionCacheEviction  #7147 — deleted with Autofac, not moved; it purged Autofac's caches; no caller outside core
